From c87374c4c6f11358c708f8df0dcbeccfccf9846a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:56:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pvr: build a fragment shader variant without the colour write
 enable select

zink makes the colour write enables dynamic state for every pipeline, so every
fragment shader ends with a read of the framebuffer under an ordering lock and
a select between the old and the new colour, even though nearly every draw
writes all outputs. That costs 5-18% on light fragment shaders.

Build a second fragment shader for graphics pipelines whose colour write
enables can leave an output masked: the same NIR lowered with the new
pco_fs_data.no_cwe flag (the preprocess then does not set
meta_present.color_write_enable), translated, encoded and uploaded with the
existing helpers by swapping the primary and alternate slots. The variant is
dropped if it spills, if the shader has no colour write enable mask, or if the
two builds do not agree on coefficients, uses, multiview and tile buffers.

At draw time pvr_gfx_select_fs_variant() picks the variant when no output the
shader writes is masked (!pvr_fs_cwe_reads_fb) and reports whether the choice
changed; the caller marks the fragment descriptors dirty after it recomputed
them from the pipeline bind, so a flip always re-emits the fragment state.
Changes of the rasterizer discard state also mark them dirty. Everything that
reads the fragment shader data or state goes through pvr_gfx_fs_data() and
pvr_gfx_fs_state(); the shared register count is the maximum of both builds.
The variant is freed by one helper on destroy and on the error paths of the
pipeline compile.

glmark2 off-screen (zink), noaltfs -> default: loop 764 -> 877, desktop shadow
277 -> 327, effect2d 445 -> 505, jellyfish 248 -> 270, shadow 283 -> 314,
function 576 -> 590 FPS. CTS cwe2, robust, ubo, nullimg, pco, cf (without the
8-bit subgroup vote cases that hang the compiler on every build), cf2, tfbc2,
loops, compute, caselist 1-3, dr_list, rp_extra and a 12000-case sample give
the same results as before; the few single cases that differed while four test
processes shared the GPU pass when run alone on every build. glmark2
--validate 27/0, and a Vulkan test that flips the colour write enable between
draws of one pipeline passes. PVR_DEBUG=noaltfs turns it off.
